<p>R1 (2026-10-28, session S15): formatting retrofit pass under the S10 charter. Mathematics converted to MathJax TeX with balanced inline delimiters and zero dollar-sign delimiters — every formula inline, because the R0 page carried no centered display equations; the head gained the standard MathJax loader block. Three figures added with machine-checked geometry — Fig P05.1 (the three surds on the √2-number line, with the exact square check \((\sqrt{50} - \sqrt{18} + \sqrt{8})^2 = 32 = (4\sqrt{2})^2\)); Fig P05.2 (the powers of 3 walking the seven residue teams mod 7 in the cycle \(3 \to 2 \to 6 \to 4 \to 5 \to 1\), the 77th step landing on team 5 since \(77 = 6 \cdot 12 + 5\)); Fig P05.3 (the conic family \(x^2 + Bxy + y^2 = 1\) at B = 0, 1, 2, 3 — circle, tilted oval, the collapse into two parallel lines, and the unbounded hyperbola with the Pell-manufactured lattice points (0, 1), (−3, 1) and (−1, 3) marked). Receipts: tag-stripped text diff against R0 shows only math-notation and figure additions; every numeric claim re-verified against the R0 lab output by a fresh verifier engine (labs/p05-format-pass.js, output recorded as labs/p05-format-pass-output.txt); SVG checks passed (viewBox present, no external references). Run history: the first figure assembly carried two layout defects, caught in review before the lab ran and fixed by regeneration — the two in-SVG note texts overran the house width limit for rendered notes, and one branch plus one witness dot of the conic figure escaped its panel frame into the neighbouring panel; all three figures were then machine-verified from the page bytes (on-curve geometry, polar node positions, panel containment) by ten fresh verifier pieces with zero shared code with the R0 engine. Three verifier-side defects were caught and fixed honestly during the lab (a line-count convention, a figure-id expectation, a copied product assertion); no mathematical check of the page ever failed, and every R0 receipt number reproduced. One genuine R0 prose defect was found and recorded, not fixed here: block 5's stated reason for the boundedness inequality claims an exact identity that holds only as a lower bound; the inequality itself is true and its receipt reproduces — flagged as a candidate for a future revision. No mathematical content was added, removed, or altered.</p>
